    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193459": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Statistics and Data Science (Tenure-Track) 2026",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Associate Professor of Statistics and Data Science (Tenure-Track) 2026 - 2027 University of Pennsylvania: The Wharton School: The Wharton School - Statistics and Data Science Location Philadelphia, PA Open Date Sep 16, 2026 Description The Department of Statistics and Data Science of the Wharton School, University of Pennsylvania, is seeking applicants for a full-time, tenure-track Associate Professor position. The appointment is expected to begin July 1, 2027. Qualifications Applicants must show outstanding capacity and achievement in research, as well as excellent teaching and communication skills. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent from an accredited institution. Application Instructions To apply, please submit the following materials through our online application system: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Statements on research and teaching. Up to 3 selected publications or preprints if available (optional). For full consideration, candidates are encouraged to have all required application documents submitted by November 15, 2026. Any questions can be sent to statistics.recruit@wharton.upenn.edu. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement The University of Pennsylvania is an equal opportunity employer. Candidates are considered for employment without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, religion, creed, national origin (including shared ancestry or ethnic characteristics), citizenship status, age, disability, veteran status or any class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensor