    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193819": {
      "title": "Orthopaedic Surgery Sports Medicine @ PPMC - AC Track, Assoc/Full Professor",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Orthopaedic Surgery Sports Medicine @ PPMC - AC Track, Assoc/Full Professor University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location Philadelphia, PA Open Date Sep 22, 2026 Deadline Sep 22, 2028 at 11:59 PM Eastern Time Description The Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Sports Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. They must also be certified by the American Board of Orthopedic Surgery or eligible for such certification. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical and didactic instruction of medical students, fellows, and orthopedic surgery residents. Clinical responsibilities may include building a practice in sports medicine at Presbyterian Medical Center with additional duties in orthopedic surgery depending on candidate training and may include on call responsibilities. Applicants who have completed an accredited sports medicine fellowship are preferred. The faculty appointment will be in the Department of Orthopedic Surgery. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement The University of Pennsylvania is an equal opportunity employer. Candidates are considered for employment without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, religion, creed, national origin (including shared ancestry or ethnic characteris